                        "entry_id": "a859e86f-bb4b-3d47-b637-58fbc4cc4769",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An act of rumination or cogitation."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f991be61-00da-47b2-8f0d-616886b7f96f",
                                "sense_id": "46c67a68-673c-3efd-bcbb-97926f035e32",
                                "text": "Now all his ponderings, however excursive, wheeled round Isabel as their center; and back to her they came again from every excursion; and again derived some new, small germs for wonderment."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "45970513-16ae-46dc-bf86-f2b8a2687380",
                                "sense_id": "46c67a68-673c-3efd-bcbb-97926f035e32",
                                "text": "Alas, it looked yesterday, when the Legislature returned to business, as if Premier Dalton McGuinty's peculiar maunderings and ponderings of the past several weeks risk making him just that."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
